  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Put a design decision to the reviewer as a card, as \`baesian file\` does. Give the card's fields; card_template shows them with their notes. Returns the card's ID and level, what the gate did with it (shown at a level, or held back: then go ahead with your pick, as provisional), near-match topics and warnings. A blocking card: call wait_for_verdict before building on it; a hard one: never proceed without a verdict. If the decision may already be on file, the error is possible_duplicate, with the matches: attach to an open one, follow a decided one, or file with new set, giving supersedes when you argue against a decision.",
