    "description": "Wait for the reviewer to answer a card, as \`baesian wait\` does: one call lasts at most 100 seconds. Returns next: use (resolved: use the decision), read (answered otherwise: read the comment, then revise or withdraw), proceed (no verdict in time: proceed provisionally on your pick), park (no verdict on a hard card: don't proceed; park the task or stop), again (the reviewer is still there: call it again), or go (held back by the repo's preferences: go ahead with your pick, as provisional; it counts as settled at merge). The whole wait lasts the timeout, across calls.",
